{title: Trust and Obey}
{title_ko: 예수 따라가며}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 449장}
{artist: John H. Sammis / Daniel B. Towner}
{genre: Hymn, Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{key_original: F}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]When we walk with the Lord in the [D]light of His Word
What a [A7]glory He [D]sheds on our [G]way
While we [G]do His good will, He a[D]bides with us still
And with [A7]all who will [D]trust and o[G]bey
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Trust and o[C]bey, for there's [G]no other way
To be [G]happy in [D]Jesus, but to trust and o[G]bey
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Not a shadow can rise, not a [D]cloud in the skies
But His [A7]smile quickly [D]drives it a[G]way
Not a [G]doubt or a fear, not a [D]sigh or a tear
Can a[A7]bide while we [D]trust and o[G]bey
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Not a burden we bear, not a [D]sorrow we share
But our [A7]toil He doth [D]richly re[G]pay
Not a [G]grief or a loss, not a [D]frown or a cross
But is [A7]blest if we [D]trust and o[G]bey
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]But we never can prove the de[D]lights of His love
Until [A7]all on the [D]altar we [G]lay
For the [G]favor He shows, and the [D]joy He bestows
Are for [A7]them who will [D]trust and o[G]bey
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Then in fellowship sweet we will [D]sit at His feet
Or we'll [A7]walk by His [D]side in the [G]way
What He [G]says we will do, where He [D]sends we will go
Never [A7]fear, only [D]trust and o[G]bey
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
